							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "The virtual machine reserves a heap of {{gtExample:GtMemoryMetrics class>>totalHeapSize|label=#humanReadableIsqByteSize}}. Most of it is the old space ({{gtExample:GtMemoryMetrics class>>totalOldSpaceSize|label=#humanReadableIsqByteSize}}), of which {{gtExample:GtMemoryMetrics class>>totalFreeOldSpaceSize|label=#humanReadableIsqByteSize}} are free. New objects are first allocated in the eden of the new space ({{gtExample:GtMemoryMetrics class>>totalEdenSize|label=#humanReadableIsqByteSize}})."
						}
					]
				},
